export default "## Euki Is Genuinely Free and Genuinely Private\n\nEuki charges nothing and does not monetize user data. No ad tier, no data licensing, no paid upgrade. Reproductive health nonprofits fund it. It uses on-device storage and requires no account.\n\nFor users who need a free period tracker with real privacy, Euki is the strongest option available. It is a good app.\n\n## The Funding Model Question\n\nEuki's strength is also its limitation. Nonprofit funding means development is driven by grant cycles, not user demand. When a grant ends, development can slow or stop. The app can fall behind on iOS and Android updates. Features that paying users would fund, like cross-device sync, are not priorities in a grant model.\n\nThis is not a criticism of Euki's mission. It is how nonprofit software works under budget constraints.\n\nSeveral reproductive health apps have gone stale or stopped working when their funding ended. Users who built their tracking history in those apps lost it.\n\n## What Floriva's Subscription Adds\n\nFloriva uses the same approach as Euki: data stays on your device, no account required, nothing on a server. The subscription funds:\n\n- Encrypted cross-device sync (your data, readable only on your devices)\n- Active iOS and Android development\n- Long-term product continuity\n\nIf $0 is the requirement, Euki is a solid choice. If a paid subscription works for you, Floriva adds sync and a sustainable roadmap.";
